        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dee88a4b-8097-56a5-ab2c-5dab67a1ae36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Gregory, Joseph McCarthy\n- Roles: Sen. John Iselin, General Ursus, Inspector Frank Luger\n- Works: The Manchurian Candidate, Beneath the Planet of the Apes, Barney Miller\n- Topics: McCarthyism, Cold War fears of Communist subversion\n\nFacts:\n- Beginning in 1950, Joseph McCarthy became the most visible public face of a period in the United States when Cold War tensions fueled fears of widespread Communist subversion.\n- James Gregory was an American character actor born on December 23, 1911, and he died on September 16, 2002.\n- James Gregory was known for his deep, gravelly voice and for playing brash roles.\n- In 1962, James Gregory played the McCarthy-like Senator John Iselin in The Manchurian Candidate.\n- In 1970, James Gregory played General Ursus in Beneath the Planet of the Apes.\n- From 1975 to 1982, James Gregory played Inspector Frank Luger in the television sitcom Barney Miller.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
